---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Section from '../../components/ui/Section.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/ui/PageHeader.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd, webPageLd } from '../../config/seo';

const pageDescription =
  'What data foxelabs.com collects, why, who processes it, and the rights you have over it.';

// Single source of truth for the visible date and the schema's dateModified.
const updatedIso = '2026-08-27';
const updated = new Date(updatedIso + 'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Foxe Labs"
  description={pageDescription}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/legal/privacy' },
    ]),
    webPageLd({
      name: 'Privacy Policy',
      description: pageDescription,
      url: '/legal/privacy',
      dateModified: updatedIso,
    }),
  ]}
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="track-hub">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Legal"
      title="Privacy Policy"
      lead="We collect as little as we can get away with. Here's exactly what we collect, why, and who touches it."
      narrow
    />
    <Section reveal={false}>
      <article class="prose-foxe max-w-3xl">
        <p class="font-mono text-[12px]" style="color: var(--ink-dim);">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          This policy explains how <strong>Foxe Labs LLP</strong> ("we", "us"), based in
          Kerala, India, handles personal data collected through
          <a href="/">foxelabs.com</a> and our software services. For anything in this
          policy, you can reach us at
          <a href="mailto:support@foxelabs.com">support@foxelabs.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What we collect, and why</h2>
        <h3>Contact form</h3>
        <p>
          When you write to us through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, we
          receive the name, email address, and message you submit. It is delivered to
          our inbox by <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend</a>,
          our email delivery provider, and used only to reply to you.
        </p>
        <h3>Waitlist</h3>
        <p>
          Joining a product waitlist stores your email address so we can tell you when
          the product launches. That's the only thing it's used for, and every email we
          send includes a way to opt out.
        </p>
        <h3>Purchases</h3>
        <p>
          Paid plugins are sold through
          <a href="https://freemius.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Freemius</a>,
          the merchant of record. Freemius collects your name, email, billing details,
          and payment information under its own
          <a href="https://freemius.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
          We receive your name, email, license details, and order metadata so we can
          deliver updates and support — <strong>we never see or store your card
          numbers</strong>.
        </p>
        <h3>Plugin usage data</h3>
        <p>
          Our WordPress plugins do not phone home by default. If a plugin offers
          opt-in usage tracking (via the Freemius SDK), it collects data only after you
          explicitly allow it, and you can opt out at any time from the plugin's
          account screen.
        </p>
        <h3>Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> measures page views and basic
          performance for every page on this site. It is cookieless and does not
          fingerprint or track individuals across sites — see
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's overview</a>
          and their <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand how the site is
          used — pages visited, approximate location, device and browser type. Google
          Analytics sets cookies and processes data under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
          We use it for aggregate statistics only; we do not use advertising features,
          and we never sell data to anyone.
        </p>
        <h3>Server logs</h3>
        <p>
          Our host, <a href="https://vercel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel</a>,
          keeps standard server logs (IP address, request URL, timestamp) for security
          and debugging. These rotate automatically.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The site itself sets no cookies for browsing, reading the blog, or using the
          docs, and our Cloudflare analytics is cookieless. Cookies come from two
          places: Google Analytics (measurement) and the Freemius checkout when you
          make a purchase (session and fraud prevention). You can block cookies in
          your browser without breaking the site.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
        <p>
          We don't sell, rent, or trade personal data. Full stop. Data is shared only
          with the processors named above — Resend (email delivery), Freemius
          (checkout and licensing), Google and Cloudflare (analytics), and Vercel
          (hosting) — each
          bound by its own privacy terms, and each receiving only what its job
          requires. We would also disclose data if a valid legal order compelled it.
        </p>

        <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact messages</strong> — kept in our inbox as long as needed to handle your request and reasonable follow-ups.</li>
          <li><strong>Waitlist emails</strong> — until the launch mails go out or you unsubscribe, whichever comes first.</li>
          <li><strong>Order and license records</strong> — for the life of your license plus what tax law requires us to retain.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — per Google Analytics' retention settings, in aggregate form.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live — including under India's Digital Personal Data
          Protection Act and the EU/UK GDPR — you may have the right to access,
          correct, export, or delete your personal data, and to withdraw consent where
          processing is based on it. To exercise any of these, email
          <a href="mailto:support@foxelabs.com">support@foxelabs.com</a> — no forms, no
          hoops. We'll respond within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Data transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Our processors (Vercel, Resend, Freemius, Google) operate globally, so data
          may be processed outside your country, including in the United States. Each
          provider maintains recognized safeguards for international transfers.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Our site and products are not directed at children under 18, and we don't
          knowingly collect their data. If you believe a child has given us personal
          data, contact us and we'll delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          When our data practices change — a new tool, a dropped provider — we'll
          update this page and the date at the top. Significant changes will be called
          out on the page itself.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions or requests:
          <a href="mailto:support@foxelabs.com">support@foxelabs.com</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
